<%# Layout for the communicator care plan PDF (Communicators::GenerateCarePlan).

    A separate layout+template pair rather than a branch inside
    layouts/pdf_printable.html.erb — the same rule that keeps pdf_marketing and
    pdf_printable apart. Two reasons here, and the second is load-bearing:

    1. render_wrappers_spec.rb asserts against pdf_printable's rendered HTML, so
       editing it to serve a second document changes bytes that spec reads.
    2. pdf_printable is architecturally a FIXED-PAGE layout — `@page { margin: 0 }`
       plus `.sheet { height: 11in; overflow: hidden }`. The `sheet` SIZE of the
       care plan is however many pages the parent's answers come to, and a fixed
       height would silently discard the rest. (The `half` and `wallet` sizes
       below ARE fixed single pages — closer in spirit to pdf_printable — but
       they still share this layout so all three sizes share one design system
       and one set of partials.)

    The brand tokens below are deliberately DUPLICATED from pdf_printable rather
    than extracted into a shared partial: extracting would change the byte
    content of that layout's <style> block, which is the thing its spec reads.
    If you edit one of the SHARED tokens (the ones pdf_printable also defines),
    edit it there too. --brand-gradient-hairline below is NOT one of those — it
    is new to this redesign and has no pdf_printable counterpart, so it lives
    only here.

    Two rails carry over unchanged from pdf_printable:

    1. Nothing is fetched over the network at render time. Nunito is inlined by
       Boards::Printables::Fonts; anything fetched mid-render fails silently
       into a fallback and nobody notices until it ships. (The avatar is a
       data: URI resolved BEFORE the render, so it doesn't break this. Icons are
       inline SVG — see CarePlanIcons — for the same reason.)
    2. Every colour is print-exact — print-color-adjust on html and body.

    NOTE ON @page: there is deliberately no `margin` here for the `sheet` size —
    Grover supplies the page margin, because Chrome renders the header/footer in
    a SEPARATE document that is clipped to nothing unless the page reserves
    margin for it. Adding `@page { margin: 0 }` — the obvious thing to copy from
    pdf_printable — makes the page numbers vanish with no error. `half` and
    `wallet` have no header/footer at all (a folded card gets no page numbers),
    so GenerateCarePlan passes `margin: 0` to Grover for those sizes instead, and
    their CSS positions content against the full untrimmed page. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Care plan</title>

    <style>
      <%= Boards::Printables::Fonts.face_css %>

      :root {
        --navy: #13496f;
        --blue-mid: #0163aa;
        --cyan: #4ECDE6;
        --magenta: #C857E8;
        --cream: #FBF7F1;
        --ink: #1A1A1A;

        --cream-deep: #F3EADC;
        --cyan-tint: #E4F7FB;
        --magenta-tint: #F8EAFD;
        --brand-gradient: linear-gradient(135deg, #4ECDE6 0%, #0163AA 55%, #C857E8 100%);
        /* The redesign's hairline/ring gradient — 4-stop, horizontal. Kept as
           its own token rather than repointing --brand-gradient at it, so the
           token this file shares with pdf_printable stays byte-identical. */
        --brand-gradient-hairline: linear-gradient(90deg, #4ECDE6 0%, #0163AA 38%, #C857E8 72%, #FFC24B 100%);

        --rule: #E2E1DD;
        --muted: #5A5A5A;
        --alert: #B3261E;
        --alert-tint: #FDECEA;

        /* Per-section accent + tint. Keyed by CarePlanDocument's STYLE_KEYS
           suffix (comm/care/meal/sens/move/trav) — a custom section maps to
           "trav" rather than getting a colour of its own; see the note there. */
        --s-comm: #0163AA; --s-comm-t: #E6F0F9; --s-comm-chip: #0B4B7F;
        --s-care: #B23BD1; --s-care-t: #F8EAFD; --s-care-chip: #7B2394;
        --s-meal: #B0700A; --s-meal-t: #FBF1DE; --s-meal-chip: #7C4E06;
        --s-sens: #6D3BE0; --s-sens-t: #EEE9FD; --s-sens-chip: #4B24A8;
        --s-move: #0E8C80; --s-move-t: #E1F4F2; --s-move-chip: #08635A;
        --s-trav: #13496F; --s-trav-t: #E7EDF3; --s-trav-chip: #0F3B5A;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

      html, body {
        -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
        print-color-adjust: exact;
      }

      body {
        font-family: Nunito, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: #fff;
        font-size: 9.5pt;
        line-height: 1.4;
        /* A parent's own free text has no guaranteed word breaks — a run of
           digits, a URL, or (in the fixture that caught this) a maxed-out
           300-character short_text field with no spaces at all. Without this
           a long unbroken token overflows its box instead of wrapping, and on
           the fixed-height half/wallet sizes `overflow: hidden` makes the
           excess vanish silently rather than merely spill visibly. */
        overflow-wrap: break-word;
      }

      @page { size: letter; }

      /* ---- Page-break behaviour (the `sheet` size only) ----

         A whole care section card is atomic: `break-inside: avoid` (on .card,
         below, alongside the rest of the design). That is safe because a
         section is half-width and its fields print one line each — the
         tallest realistic one (Meals, four fields, one a 300-character
         short_text) is around 1.1in in a column. If one ever does outgrow a
         column Chrome splits it rather than clipping it, which is the
         acceptable failure. Do not add `column-fill: auto`. */
      .row, .item, .contact { break-inside: avoid; }
      p { orphans: 3; widows: 3; }

      /* ---- Page frame (the `sheet` size only) ----
         Repeats on EVERY page: Chrome paints a position:fixed element once per
         sheet in the print path, and its insets resolve against the page's
         content box — inside the @page margins Grover supplies. A bordered
         wrapper div cannot do this. It fragments, so the top edge would draw
         only on page 1 and the bottom edge only on the last, leaving the middle
         sheets framed on two sides.

         inset MUST be 0. Negative insets look like the way to buy breathing
         room between the frame and the text, but Chrome clips the fixed layer
         to the page content box and the frame then paints on NO page at all —
         a silent no-op that looks like the CSS was ignored. Verified at -4pt,
         not just at the larger values that might plausibly overflow the paper. */
      .page-frame {
        position: fixed;
        inset: 0;
        border: 0.75pt solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 10pt;
      }

      /* Clearance inside .page-frame, on the `sheet` size's own content
         wrapper rather than on body — half and wallet paint their own fixed
         pages and must not inherit this padding.

         Two mechanisms, because they cover different pages: this padding for
         page 1 (laid out once, at the start of the flow), and .card's own
         padding-top (below) for every later page — a card is atomic
         (break-inside: avoid), so whatever a continuation page starts with is
         always the top of one, flush against .page-frame, and its own padding
         survives the fragmentation break where a margin would be truncated. */
      .sheet-content { padding: 9pt 11pt; }

      /* ---- Preview rendering (the PNG thumbnail only) ----

         The thumbnail is a SCREENSHOT, not a print. Grover's `margin:` option
         is what insets the `sheet` size's content on paper, and a screenshot
         gets none of it — so without this the frame hugs the image edge and
         the text starts hard against it, which is not what prints.

         Chrome emulates PRINT media for to_pdf and SCREEN media for to_png, so
         a @media screen block reaches the preview and nothing else. That is
         the whole mechanism: if anyone ever sets `emulate_media: "screen"` on
         the PDF path these rules would start applying to paper and the sheet
         would be double-margined. Don't.

         Keep these values identical to the `sheet` margins in
         GenerateCarePlan#letter_options. `half` and `wallet` render at
         `margin: 0` and lay themselves out in physical units against the full
         untrimmed page, so at a Letter-sized viewport they already match the
         PDF exactly and must NOT be padded — neither selector below exists in
         those two templates, which is what keeps them out of it. */
      @media screen {
        .page-frame { inset: 0.5in 0.5in 0.55in; }
        .sheet-content { padding: calc(9pt + 0.5in) calc(11pt + 0.5in) calc(9pt + 0.55in); }
      }

      /* ================= identity header (sheet + half) ================= */
      .topbar { height: 6pt; background: var(--brand-gradient-hairline); margin: -9pt -11pt 0; }

      .identity {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11pt;
        padding: 10pt 11pt; margin-top: 10pt;
        background: var(--cream); border-radius: 9pt; border: 0.75pt solid var(--cream-deep);
      }
      .identity .portrait, .fid .portrait {
        flex: none; border-radius: 999pt;
        background: var(--brand-gradient-hairline);
      }
      .identity .portrait { width: 54pt; height: 54pt; padding: 2pt; }
      .identity .portrait img, .fid .portrait img {
        width: 100%; height: 100%; border-radius: 999pt; object-fit: cover;
        object-position: 50% 22%; display: block; border: 1.25pt solid #fff;
      }
      .identity .who, .fid .who { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
      .identity .doctype, .fid .doctype {
        font-size: 6.3pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 1.5pt;
      }
      .identity h1 {
        font-size: 17pt; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--navy);
      }
      /* Pronouns sit on their own line under the name — inline with the h1
         they compete with it for the same optical baseline and read like a
         suffix. Called out specifically in review. */
      .pronoun {
        display: inline-block; font-size: 6.3pt; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue-mid); background: #fff;
        border: 0.75pt solid #CBDCEA; border-radius: 999pt; padding: 1pt 6pt; margin-top: 3pt;
      }
      /* The "says" line is a caption under the name, not a second headline.
         It ran at nearly the body size and in two weights of navy, so on the
         half size it read as a subtitle competing with the h1 it sits under —
         the name is what a reader is looking for first. Sized down and set in
         one weight here; .fid scales it a little for the bigger panel. */
      .identity .says, .fid .says {
        font-size: 7.4pt; font-weight: 600; color: #4A4845; margin-top: 2.5pt; line-height: 1.25;
      }
      .says em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }
      .says.muted { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; }

      .qrblock { flex: none; text-align: center; width: 62pt; }
      .qrblock .frame {
        background: #fff; border: 0.75pt solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6pt;
        padding: 3pt; line-height: 0; display: inline-block;
      }
      .qrblock img { width: 46pt; height: 46pt; display: block; }
      .qrblock .cap { font-size: 5.8pt; font-weight: 800; color: var(--navy); margin-top: 2pt; line-height: 1.15; }
      .qrblock .url { font-size: 5pt; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); word-break: break-all; line-height: 1.15; margin-top: 1pt; }

      /* ================= at a glance (sheet + half) ================= */
      /* Two cells — allergies and how I talk. The third, "Call first", is gone:
         see the note in _care_plan_glance.html.erb. */
      .glance {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0;
        margin-top: 8pt; border: 1pt solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8pt; overflow: hidden;
      }
      .glance .cell { padding: 6pt 9pt; border-left: 1pt solid var(--rule); }
      .glance .cell:first-child { border-left: 0; }
      .glance .k {
        font-size: 6pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 1.5pt;
      }
      .glance .v { font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.15; color: var(--navy); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
      .glance .cell.danger { background: var(--alert-tint); }
      .glance .cell.danger .k, .glance .cell.danger .v { color: var(--alert); }
      .glance .sub { font-size: 6.8pt; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 1pt; }

      /* ================= emergency (sheet + half) ================= */
      .emergency {
        margin-top: 9pt; border: 0.75pt solid #EBD4D2; border-left: 3pt solid var(--alert);
        border-radius: 7pt; padding: 7pt 10pt; background: #fff;
      }
      .sec-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; }
      .sec-head h2 { font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .sec-head .line { flex: 1; height: 1pt; }
      .emergency .sec-head h2 { color: var(--alert); }
      .emergency .sec-head .line { background: rgba(179, 38, 30, 0.22); }

      .egrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2pt 16pt; }
      .egrid .f { font-size: 9pt; line-height: 1.35; }
      .egrid .f .k {
        font-size: 6.8pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--alert); margin-right: 4pt;
      }
      .egrid .f.wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
      .not-provided {
        grid-column: 1 / -1; font-size: 7pt; font-style: italic; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 3pt;
      }

      .contacts { margin-top: 6pt; padding-top: 5pt; border-top: 1pt solid rgba(179, 38, 30, 0.22); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4pt 12pt; }
      .contact {
        background: var(--cream); border: 0.75pt solid var(--cream-deep); border-radius: 6pt; padding: 5pt 8pt;
      }
      .contact.plain { background: none; border: 0; padding: 0; }
      .contact .name { font-size: 8pt; font-weight: 800; color: var(--navy); }
      .contact .rel { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
      /* The single most important glyph sequence on the sheet — it used to be
         the same size as "Handwashing". */
      .contact .phone { font-size: 14.5pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.01em; white-space: nowrap; display: block; }

      /* ================= day-to-day: heading + section cards (sheet + half) ================= */
      .care-heading {
        font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: 900; color: var(--navy); text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.09em; margin: 11pt 0 6pt; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6pt;
      }
      .care-heading::after { content: ""; flex: 1; height: 1.5pt; background: var(--cyan); }

      .cols { column-count: 2; column-gap: 16pt; }

      .card {
        break-inside: avoid; -webkit-column-break-inside: avoid;
        border: 0.75pt solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8pt; padding: 7pt 9pt 8pt;
        margin: 0 0 8pt; background: #fff;
      }
      .card .hd { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; }
      .card .ico { flex: none; width: 15pt; height: 15pt; border-radius: 4.5pt; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
      .card .ico svg { width: 9pt; height: 9pt; display: block; fill: none; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
      .card h3 { font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }

      .row { margin-top: 4pt; }
      .row:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
      .row .k {
        display: block; font-size: 6pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 2pt;
      }
      .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2.5pt; }
      .chip { font-size: 7.5pt; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.25; padding: 1.5pt 5.5pt; border-radius: 4pt; white-space: nowrap; }
      /* Middle overflow tier on the half size: comma-joined text instead of
         chips, roughly half the height per row. */
      .row .text { font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3; color: #332F2B; }
      .say { font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3; color: #332F2B; }

      .s-comm .ico { background: var(--s-comm-t); } .s-comm .ico svg { stroke: var(--s-comm); }
      .s-comm h3 { color: var(--s-comm); } .s-comm .chip { background: var(--s-comm-t); color: var(--s-comm-chip); }
      .s-care .ico { background: var(--s-care-t); } .s-care .ico svg { stroke: var(--s-care); }
      .s-care h3 { color: var(--s-care); } .s-care .chip { background: var(--s-care-t); color: var(--s-care-chip); }
      .s-meal .ico { background: var(--s-meal-t); } .s-meal .ico svg { stroke: var(--s-meal); }
      .s-meal h3 { color: var(--s-meal); } .s-meal .chip { background: var(--s-meal-t); color: var(--s-meal-chip); }
      .s-sens .ico { background: var(--s-sens-t); } .s-sens .ico svg { stroke: var(--s-sens); }
      .s-sens h3 { color: var(--s-sens); } .s-sens .chip { background: var(--s-sens-t); color: var(--s-sens-chip); }
      .s-move .ico { background: var(--s-move-t); } .s-move .ico svg { stroke: var(--s-move); }
      .s-move h3 { color: var(--s-move); } .s-move .chip { background: var(--s-move-t); color: var(--s-move-chip); }
      .s-trav .ico { background: var(--s-trav-t); } .s-trav .ico svg { stroke: var(--s-trav); }
      .s-trav h3 { color: var(--s-trav); } .s-trav .chip { background: var(--s-trav-t); color: var(--s-trav-chip); }

      .item { padding: 1.5pt 0; border-top: 0.6pt solid var(--rule); font-size: 8.5pt; line-height: 1.35; }
      .item .k { font-weight: 800; }

      .muted { color: var(--muted); }

      .footnote {
        margin-top: 10pt; padding-top: 5pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid var(--rule);
        font-size: 6.8pt; color: var(--muted); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8pt;
      }
      .footnote .mark { width: 13pt; height: 13pt; display: block; flex: none; }

      /* ================= fold mechanics (half + wallet) =================
         Both sizes print SINGLE-SIDED. The sheet is divided into two faces;
         the half that becomes the back is authored upright and rotated 180deg
         in the print layout, so folding print-side-OUT lands it reading
         correctly.

         Rotating about the horizontal fold axis flips content vertically AND
         puts it on the reverse face; turning the folded card over to read the
         back then mirrors it horizontally. Vertical flip + horizontal mirror
         = 180deg, so pre-rotating by 180deg is exactly the correction needed.
         Never "fix" this rotation later — see the handoff doc's fold-mechanics
         section for the full derivation. There is no screen-review toggle to
         un-rotate here (the mockup's was explicitly a review affordance, not a
         feature) — verify a folded print by folding a printed copy. */
      .flip { transform: rotate(180deg); }

      .foldrule { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; height: 0; border-top: 1pt dashed #A9A5B6; z-index: 5; }
      .foldrule span {
        position: absolute; right: 0.42in; left: auto; top: -5pt; background: #fff; padding: 0 6pt;
        font-size: 6pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #7C7890;
      }

      /* ================= half-page fold card ================= */
      /* The fold is at the geometric middle of the sheet — 5.5in of 11in — and
         each panel is the same 5.5in tall, so a printed copy creases exactly
         in half. Never trade that for a taller face: the crease is what a
         reader lines up when they fold it back along an existing fold. */
      .foldsheet { width: 8.5in; height: 11in; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
      .fpanel { height: 5.5in; padding: 0 0.5in 0.3in; position: relative; overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
      /* A panel is a fixed-height flex column with `overflow: hidden`, which
         means an over-full face does not simply spill — the flex algorithm
         SHRINKS whichever child can give, and that child then clips its own
         content silently. It picked the glance strip, so "Allergies / How I
         talk" printed as a row of half-height cells with the values sliced
         through the middle. Nothing on either face may shrink: if a face is
         over-full the honest failure is content running past the fold, which
         is visible, and the overflow ladder is what prevents it. */
      .fpanel > * { flex: none; }
      /* Gradient sits on each face's OUTER edge, not at the fold — two bars
         meeting at the crease made a 12pt band that got creased in half and
         collided with the fold marks. */
      .fbar { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; height: 6pt; background: var(--brand-gradient-hairline); }

      .fid { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12pt; padding: 9pt 0 7pt; }
      .fid .portrait { width: 68pt; height: 68pt; padding: 2.5pt; }
      .fid .portrait img { border: 2pt solid #fff; }
      .fid h1 { font-size: 23pt; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--navy); }
      .fid .says { font-size: 8.6pt; margin-top: 3pt; }
      .fid .qrblock { width: 78pt; }
      .fid .qrblock img { width: 58pt; height: 58pt; }
      .fid .qrblock .cap { font-size: 6pt; }
      .fid .qrblock .url { font-size: 5.4pt; }

      /* The front face is the tight one — identity, glance, emergency and the
         footnote all have to land inside 5.5in for a profile with three
         contacts and a long notes field. Everything below is sized against
         that budget; trimming the glance or the contact cards is what buys
         room, never letting a child shrink (see `.fpanel > *`). */
      .fpanel .glance { margin-top: 7pt; }
      .fpanel .glance .v { font-size: 12.5pt; }
      .fpanel .glance .k { font-size: 6.5pt; }
      .fpanel .glance .sub { font-size: 7.5pt; }
      .fpanel .glance .cell { padding: 6pt 11pt; }

      .fpanel .emergency { margin-top: 7pt; padding: 6pt 10pt; }
      .fpanel .contact { padding: 4pt 8pt; }
      .fpanel .contact .phone { font-size: 15.5pt; }
      .fpanel .contact .name { font-size: 8.5pt; }

      .ffoot { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 7pt; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid var(--rule); }
      .ffoot p { flex: 1; font-size: 6.8pt; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.3; }
      .ffoot p b { color: #3B3A38; font-weight: 800; }
      .ffoot img { width: 14pt; height: 14pt; flex: none; }
      .ffoot .full-plan-note { display: block; font-size: 6.5pt; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-top: 2pt; }

      /* Back face is tighter than the sheet — 4.5in of usable height.
         .fbody takes whatever the care block doesn't use and splits it above
         and below, so a profile that answered three sections prints as a
         balanced face rather than a band of cards jammed against one edge
         with an inch of white under it. The footnote stays pinned to the
         bottom (its own margin-top: auto) either way. */
      /* `safe center` centres only while the content FITS. Plain `center`
         splits an overflow across both edges, which on the back face means
         spilling over the fold and onto the front — the one direction an
         over-full face must never grow. */
      .fpanel .fbody { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: safe center; }
      .fpanel .care-heading { margin: 0 0 5pt; }
      .fpanel .cols { column-gap: 16pt; }
      .fpanel .card { padding: 5.5pt 8pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; }
      .fpanel .card .hd { margin-bottom: 3pt; }
      .fpanel .row { margin-top: 3pt; }
      .fpanel .chips { gap: 2pt; }
      .fpanel .card h3 { font-size: 9.5pt; }
      .fpanel .row .k { font-size: 6pt; }
      .fpanel .chip { font-size: 7.5pt; padding: 1.5pt 5pt; }
      .fpanel .row .text, .fpanel .say { font-size: 8.5pt; }
      /* Condensed-lines tier (no chips at all — see care_plan_half's overflow
         branch). One line per section: label, then comma-joined values. */
      .fpanel .condensed-lines { margin-top: 2pt; }
      .fpanel .condensed-lines .cline { display: flex; gap: 5pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; align-items: baseline; break-inside: avoid; }
      .fpanel .condensed-lines .cline .k {
        flex: none; width: 64pt; font-size: 6pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
      }
      .fpanel .condensed-lines .cline .v {
        flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3; color: #2A2724;
      }

      /* ================= wallet fold strip ================= */
      /* Four identical strips, 2 across x 2 down, 7 x 8in of image centred on
         the untrimmed 8.5x11in page (Grover's margin: 0 for this size). The
         outer .wallet-sheet is the positioning context for both the grid and
         the cut/fold legend below it. */
      .wallet-sheet { width: 8.5in; height: 11in; position: relative; }
      .wallet-page {
        position: absolute; inset: 0;
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 3.5in); grid-template-rows: repeat(2, 4in);
        justify-content: center; align-content: center; gap: 0;
      }
      /* Each strip folds at 2in of 4in — the exact middle, same rule the half
         size's 5.5in crease follows. Both faces are sized to be FILLED: the
         front carries identity + allergies + every contact, the back carries
         the day-to-day lines. See the one-subject-per-face note in
         _care_plan_wallet_strip.html.erb. */
      .wstrip { width: 3.5in; height: 4in; position: relative; background: #fff; border: 1pt solid #B9B6C4; overflow: hidden; }
      .wstrip .half { height: 2in; position: relative; overflow: hidden; padding: 7pt 9pt; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
      /* Same rule as .fpanel > *: a fixed-height flex column with hidden
         overflow shrinks-then-clips instead of spilling, and the clip is
         silent. Nothing on a wallet face may shrink. */
      .wstrip .half > * { flex: none; }
      .wstrip .half .wtop { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; top: auto; height: 4pt; background: var(--brand-gradient-hairline); }

      .wfront .who { display: flex; gap: 7pt; align-items: center; }
      .wfront .pic { flex: none; width: 36pt; height: 36pt; border-radius: 999pt; padding: 1.5pt; background: var(--brand-gradient-hairline); }
      .wfront .pic img { width: 100%; height: 100%; border-radius: 999pt; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 22%; display: block; }
      .wfront .nm { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
      .wfront .nm h4 { font-size: 12pt; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.05; color: var(--navy); letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
      /* The live-page URL, moved off the old absolutely-positioned .wfoot at
         the bottom edge — that strip of the front is contacts now. */
      .wfront .nm .u { font-size: 4.6pt; font-weight: 700; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 1.5pt; word-break: break-all; }
      .wfront .qr { flex: none; text-align: center; width: 38pt; }
      .wfront .qr img { width: 34pt; height: 34pt; display: block; margin: 0 auto; }
      .wfront .qr .c { font-size: 4.2pt; font-weight: 800; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.04em; margin-top: 1pt; line-height: 1.1; }

      .wallergy { margin-top: 5pt; background: var(--alert-tint); border-left: 2.5pt solid var(--alert); border-radius: 4pt; padding: 3pt 6pt; }
      .wallergy .k { font-size: 5.4pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--alert); }
      .wallergy .v { font-size: 9.5pt; font-weight: 900; color: var(--alert); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }

      /* Contacts on the FRONT. One row per contact — the relationship and name
         on the left, the number right-aligned and set large, because that
         number is the whole reason the card is in someone's pocket. */
      /* margin-top: auto settles the contacts against the cut edge, so the
         face's leftover height falls between the blocks instead of pooling at
         the bottom — the whitespace this card used to print under a lone
         "Call first" line. */
      .wcontacts { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 4pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid var(--rule); }
      .wcontacts .chead {
        font-size: 5.2pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--alert); margin-bottom: 2.5pt;
      }
      .wcontacts .c { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 5pt; margin-bottom: 1.5pt; }
      .wcontacts .c .n { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-size: 5.8pt; font-weight: 800; color: var(--navy); line-height: 1.15; }
      .wcontacts .c .p { flex: none; font-size: 9.5pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; white-space: nowrap; }

      .wback .bhead {
        font-size: 5.6pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 3pt; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4pt;
      }
      .wback .bhead::after { content: ""; flex: 1; height: 1pt; background: var(--cyan); }
      /* The back is one block in a 2in face, so it centres in whatever it
         doesn't fill — same reason .fbody exists on the half size. */
      .wback .wlist { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: safe center; }
      .wlist .li { display: flex; gap: 4pt; margin-bottom: 2pt; align-items: baseline; }
      .wlist .li .k {
        flex: none; width: 52pt; font-size: 4.4pt; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.25;
      }
      .wlist .li .v { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-size: 6.6pt; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.18; color: #2A2724; }

      /* Cut/fold legend, printed once in the page margin below the 2x2 grid. */
      .wallet-legend {
        position: absolute; left: 0.5in; right: 0.5in; bottom: 0.35in;
        font-size: 6.5pt; color: var(--muted); display: flex; gap: 14pt; align-items: center;
      }
      .wallet-legend .keyline { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4pt; font-weight: 800; }
      .wallet-legend i { display: inline-block; width: 16pt; height: 0; border-top: 1pt solid #B9B6C4; }
      .wallet-legend i.dash { border-top-style: dashed; border-top-color: #A9A5B6; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
